body:
Looks like the segments get parsed in this method of url_tree.ts

```
const SEGMENT_RE = /^[^\/()?;=&#]+/;
function matchSegments(str: string): string {
  const match = str.match(SEGMENT_RE);
  return match ? match[0] : '';
}
```

Of course it won't be as simple as just removing the `=` from the regex. I'm not sure I know enough about all the url rule permutations to propose a fix.

Another effect of this is that removing of the `=` sign happens after the matching has happened.
Example:
```
// router config
{
  path: "prefix/:slug",
  component: MyComponent
}
```
Opening a url `example.com/prefix/=` matches this route and renders MyComponent. However, inside the component ActivatedRoute has an empty (`""`) value for the `slug` parameter - which fails some runtime validation in our code and throws.
